    "prompt": "Please make a 1920×1200 icon sheet for my desk-planning notebook. I want familiar objects rendered in charcoal with tonal shading; a front-facing view should make their balanced shapes easy to recognize.\n\n- Arrange exactly four separate icons in a loose 2×2 grid: an alarm clock, a roll of tape, a pencil cup, and a round desk stamp.\n- Give each object a clear vertical centerline. Its main outline and defining details should mirror across that line; keep shading balanced rather than using shadows that skew the silhouette.\n- Make the circular parts especially legible: concentric bezel and dial on the clock, outer rim and inner hole on the tape, an oval rim on the cup, and a circular collar on the stamp. Keep each ring centered on its object’s axis.\n- Put three pencils in the cup: one upright in the middle and two angled as mirror partners.",
